#lang saffron
;; docs/guides/saffron-guide.md, "Typeclasses": a method on an un-narrowed
;; `any` is a DIAGNOSTIC naming the three ways out, not a guess and not
;; uncompilable C.
;;
;; The guide quotes both the error and its help line, so both are pinned here.
;; The help text is the load-bearing half: it is what sends a reader to the
;; type-case, and an earlier version of this path had no diagnostic at all when
;; a single instance was in scope.

(defn h [x] (hash x))

(defn main [] 0)
